    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic, not an optimal solver. It repeatedly takes the vehicle that becomes free earliest and assigns it the unused ride with the best points-per-step rate among those it can still finish by their latest finish. A vehicle with no feasible ride left is dropped, since its options only shrink over time. I have not compiled or run it against any data set. The worst case is about N+F scans of N rides (roughly 10^8 simple operations), well within the time limit.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nstruct V {\n    ll t;\n    int r, c;\n    int id;\n    bool operator>(const V& o) const {\n        if (t != o.t) return t > o.t;\n        return id > o.id;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    ll R, C, F, N, B, T;\n    cin >> R >> C >> F >> N >> B >> T;\n    vector<ll> a(N), b(N), x(N), y(N), s(N), f(N), dist(N);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        cin >> a[i] >> b[i] >> x[i] >> y[i] >> s[i] >> f[i];\n        dist[i] = llabs(x[i] - a[i]) + llabs(y[i] - b[i]);\n    }\n\n    priority_queue<V, vector<V>, greater<V>> pq;\n    for (int i = 0; i < F; ++i) pq.push(V{0, 0, 0, i});\n\n    vector<char> used(N, 0);\n    vector<vector<int>> assigned(F);\n\n    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        V v = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n\n        int best = -1;\n        double bestVal = -1.0;\n        ll bestFin = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n            if (used[i]) continue;\n            ll d0 = llabs(a[i] - v.r) + llabs(b[i] - v.c);\n            ll arr = v.t + d0;\n            ll st = max(arr, s[i]);\n            ll fin = st + dist[i];\n            if (fin > f[i]) continue;\n            ll pts = dist[i] + (st == s[i] ? B : 0);\n            double val = (double)pts / (double)(fin - v.t);\n            if (best == -1 || val > bestVal ||\n                (val == bestVal && fin < bestFin)) {\n                best = i;\n                bestVal = val;\n                bestFin = fin;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (best == -1) continue; // this vehicle has no more feasible rides\n\n        used[best] = 1;\n        assigned[v.id].push_back(best);\n        pq.push(V{bestFin, (int)x[best], (int)y[best], v.id});\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    for (int i = 0; i < F; ++i) {\n        out += to_string(assigned[i].size());\n        for (int r : assigned[i]) {\n            out += ' ';\n            out += to_string(r);\n        }\n        out += '\\n';\n    }\n    cout << out;\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
